### Applications — /api/scopes/{scopeId}/applications
#
# Run auth.http's "Login" first, then scopes.http's "Create a scope" so {{scopeId}} is set.
#
# An application's owner must be a ScopeAdmin who owns the addressed scope. A User may never own one,
# so ownerId here is a person from persons.http's "Create an administrator", added as an owner.

### Register an application in a scope (UC-16) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example Application",
  "ownerId": "{{personId}}"
}

> {%
    if (response.body.data && response.body.data.id) {
        client.global.set("applicationId", response.body.data.id);
        client.log("Stored applicationId " + response.body.data.id);
    }
%}

### Read one application (UC-17) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}?includeDeleted=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List a scope's applications (UC-17) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&includeDeleted=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List a scope's applications filtered by owner (UC-17).
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications?pageNumber=1&pageSize=20&ownerId={{personId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update an application's name and owner (UC-18) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
# The new owner must also be a ScopeAdmin who owns this scope.
PUT {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example Application, renamed",
  "ownerId": "{{personId}}"
}

### Logically delete an application (UC-19) — System Admin or owning Scope Admin.
DELETE {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Hard delete an application (UC-20) — System Admin.
DELETE {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/hard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Issue a credential (UC-53) — System Admin or the Scope Admin who owns the application.
# The secret is in this response only. Store it now.
POST {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expiresAt": "2030-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

> {%
    if (response.body.data && response.body.data.id) {
        client.global.set("credentialId", response.body.data.id);
        client.global.set("applicationSecret", response.body.data.secret);
    }
%}

### List the application's credentials (UC-54).
GET {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Obtain an application token (UC-56) — anonymous; the secret authenticates.
POST {{host}}/api/applications/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}",
  "scopeId": "{{scopeId}}",
  "secret": "{{applicationSecret}}"
}

> {%
    if (response.body.data && response.body.data.token) {
        client.global.set("applicationToken", response.body.data.token);
    }
%}

### Check the application token live (UC-57).
GET {{host}}/api/applications/self
Authorization: Bearer {{applicationToken}}

### Revoke the credential (UC-55). The token above then fails the live check.
DELETE {{host}}/api/scopes/{{scopeId}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/credentials/{{credentialId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
